{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall know that HaShem your Elohim</b> etc. This connects to above: since you see that the Holy One, blessed be He, kept His promise to our fathers, one can then infer and know that He <b>is the faithful one, keeper of the covenant and the kindness</b> etc." "<b>To a thousand generations.</b> Why is this said? So that you not say: since it was not because of your multitude that HaShem desired you, but rather because of His love and His keeping the oath — what business is it of ours to toil to fulfill His commandments? He needs to fulfill His oath! Therefore it says <b>to a thousand generations</b> — that is, He will wait a thousand generations beforehand, so that no worthy generation may be found to receive the covenant and the kindness on behalf of the fathers to whom He swore." "<b>Keeper of the covenant.</b> An expression of waiting, as in 'his father kept the matter' (ואביו שמר את הדבר)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:04.342624525Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}